# chess-review — environment variables
#
# A few optional app variables exist (engine CDN base, chess.com callback
# flag, KV cache); everything else below is a conventional variable
# honoured by the Next.js / Node runtime itself (none required).
# The app builds, starts and passes its tests with no `.env` file present.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_ENGINE_BASE_URL — where the Stockfish engine files are served
# from. Default: `/engine` (same-origin, copied there by postinstall).
# Point it at a CDN directory that contains the same files
# (stockfish-19*.js/.wasm + engine-manifest.json) to host the ~191 MiB engine
# payload off your app server, e.g.:
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ENGINE_BASE_URL=https://cdn.example.com/engine
#
# The CDN must send `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` (the client fetches the
# manifest + WASM) and `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin` (or serve
# under COEP-compatible CORS). See README "Hosting the engine on a CDN".
# NOTE: this is a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable — it is inlined at build time, so set
# it before `npm run build`, not at runtime.
# `ENGINE_BASE_URL` (without the prefix) is accepted as an alias by
# next.config.js and mapped onto the canonical name.
#
# ENGINE_BUNDLE — which engine builds ship in public/engine (build-time,
# read by scripts/copy-engine.mjs at `npm ci` postinstall): all (default),
# multi+lite, lite-only, or external (ship none; pair with the CDN base
# above). See README "Deployment profiles".

# CHESSCOM_CALLBACK_ENABLED — Prompt 11. The chess.com "callback" game
# import (GET /api/chesscom?id=…) uses an unofficial endpoint; it stays
# DISABLED unless this is set to 1 (or true). When disabled the route
# answers 503 NOT_CONFIGURED and the UI offers the paste-PGN fallback.
# The username archive import (GET /api/chesscom?user=…) is unaffected.
# CHESSCOM_CALLBACK_ENABLED=1

# KV_REST_API_URL / KV_REST_API_TOKEN — Prompt 11 server cache. When both
# are present, the import routes use the Upstash Redis / Vercel KV REST
# protocol for their server-side cache (shared across serverless
# instances); otherwise an in-memory per-instance cache is used.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL / UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN are honoured as
# aliases. No SDK dependency — plain fetch against the REST protocol.
# KV_REST_API_URL=https://<your-kv-host>
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=<token>

# PORT=3000            # Port for `next start` (Next.js default: 3000).
#                      # The Playwright config sets PORT=3100 for its own
#                      # webServer; you do not need to set it yourself.
# NODE_ENV=production  # Set automatically by `next build` / `next start`.
